        },
        "title": "Invariants",
        "body": "- **One description.** A switch is described in exactly one place, the node that carries it. The card you read, the panel you edit with and the snapshot the app loads are all made from that node. None of them is a second copy.\n- **A switch names where it is written.** Every switch has a write path, such as `edge.style.arrowSize`. If a value cannot be written at a path, it is not a switch.\n- **Policies are decisions, switches are values.** When something is decided by the app rather than set, such as which view a tile shows at a given size, it is a policy, and a switch may name the policy that governs it. A threshold is not a switch.\n- **Honest about what is built.** Each switch states its status and whether a control for it exists. \"None found\" means no control turned up, not that none could exist.\n- **Panels follow the contract, not the reverse.** A control that has no switch does not ship. A switch with no control is allowed, and says so.",
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "authoring-contract"
        },
        "classRef": "tlz://twilite.zone/library/templates/page-template/classes/page-section.node-class.node"
      },
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any",
          "position": {
            "side": "top",
            "offset": 0.2
          }
        }
      ],
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
